  "note": "Chrome CPU-throttle proxy for an iPhone XS Max (414x896 @3, mobile profile); GPU work is not throttled. The host carried 28-48% unrelated load throughout, so the step-1 and step-2 builds were alternated under the same conditions instead of comparing with docs/testing/hmh-perf-crowd-baseline.json. rAF intervals are vsync-quantised (16.7/27.8/34.7/41.7 ms steps), so the per-frame work probe below is the more direct measure.",
  "change": {
    "renderer": "renderWorldProductionArt({ pass: \"static\" | \"dynamic\", cues, shimmers }); with pass omitted it draws everything exactly as before",
    "bake": "apps/hmh-reboot/src/world-static-bake.mjs, a lazy chunk fetched beside app.init. The static layers sit in two render groups that are translated per frame. It re-bakes on margin exit (320 px), zoom, view, terrain registry version, fallback blockers, town fallback visibility or decal set, bakes the bare view while the zoom animates, and corrects the tile phase for camera.groundZ.",
    "main": "Decals are drawn once per bake and move with it; the backdrop and vignette redraw on resize only; empty overlay Graphics are no longer cleared."
  },
